<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_Wasteland                                  UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/wasteland.md
    (FROZEN). One def by ruling (sheet SS0): the different wastelands (dayside basins,
    the margin, the dark scour) vary only by mutators and Inhabited injections, never
    by BiomeDef — the fall_line.md no-new-BiomeDef precedent, extended. This owned
    def carries that one def forward.

    MEASURED (sheet SS0): 1,126 tiles, arc p10/median/p90 73/90/108 (sitting exactly
    on the terminator at the median). War-legacy split (sheet SS0): Wasteland is the
    POISONED legacy — conventional radiation and chemical contamination, never
    Assailant bioweapon content (that is PoisonForest's and the Contagion's lane).

    Weather: ban 5 is explicit — "No rain (R-H1: rain falls only at the greatest
    altitudes; the Wasteland is not one)" — so Rain/RainyThunderstorm are zeroed.
    ToxRain and GrayPall (Anomaly) kept: SS4b names ash storms and radiation-halo
    storms as the standing weather (no WeatherDef yet exists for either by that
    name — SS Owed engine-feasibility — ToxRain and GrayPall are the nearest
    existing stand-ins, reflavored, not invented). Ban 7 stands: "Plasma storms
    never occur outside the terminator families" — none added here since no plasma
    WeatherDef exists to add.

    diseases trimmed to the plain vanilla suite (dropped the donor's AnimalFlu/
    AnimalPlague/OrganDecay/BMT_Disease_Mutapox): ban 4 requires every resident to be
    "visibly shaped by the contamination," and the sheet's own disease register is
    radiation/toxin, not wildlife epidemiology — left at the donor's core set rather
    than inventing a radiological disease that does not exist as a def yet (SS Owed
    "needs a dose/geiger layer").

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/wasteland.json.

    NOT this pass's scope: the dose/geiger layer; the three storm WeatherDefs (ash,
    halo, plasma); the mutator/injection palette per family (SS8 table, its own
    authoring pass); the Junkers' tipping-fee economy; the Throat.

    FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1 wave 2 (2026-09-18): waterShallowTerrain/waterDeepTerrain/
    waterMovingShallowTerrain/waterMovingChestDeepTerrain wired to the
    RUT_WastelandBrine* terrains (RUT_WastelandBrineWater.xml, this folder) instead
    of being left unset. Left unset, any water this def generates fell back to
    vanilla TerrainDefOf.WaterDeep/WaterShallow (Verse/MapGenUtility.cs:182) —
    ordinary freshwater, contradicting wave 1's "engine-dead" finding, which
    analyzed the DONOR `Wasteland` BiomeDef (unused by the live map; MEASURED via
    world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_tiles.csv, RUT_Wasteland covers all 1853 Wasteland tiles,
    bare "Wasteland" covers zero) rather than this def. Wired here anyway, toxic
    flavor and all, because the owner's mining ruling for the brine-battery
    archetype (RUT_Tekk/RUT_Drazz/RUT_BrinePlate) stands on its own merits, not as
    a workaround — see RUT_WastelandBrineDeposits.xml. oceanDeepTerrain/
    oceanShallowTerrain left unset: the pools are "basins sealed from the seas"
    (wasteland.md), never ocean-typed.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_Wasteland</defName>
    <generatesNaturally>false</generatesNaturally>
    <label>the Wasteland</label>
    <description>Where rivers die, everything they carried is concentrated into salt and brine; where the sky's exhaust falls, nothing ever washes it away. Nothing here recycles -- water doesn't leave, fallout doesn't wash, history doesn't decay. The wildlife is wretched and mutated as the rule, extremophile-odd as the exception; the danger is the ground, the air and the water, never the creatures. They merely adapt, struggle, and mostly fail.</description>
    <workerClass>BiomesPlus.BiomeWorker_Wasteland</workerClass>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>Gravel</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <mudTerrain>MarshyTerrain</mudTerrain>
    <riverbankTerrain>MarshyTerrain</riverbankTerrain>
    <waterShallowTerrain MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">RUT_WastelandBrineShallow</waterShallowTerrain>
    <waterDeepTerrain MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">RUT_WastelandBrineDeep</waterDeepTerrain>
    <waterMovingShallowTerrain MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">RUT_WastelandBrineMovingShallow</waterMovingShallowTerrain>
    <waterMovingChestDeepTerrain MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">RUT_WastelandBrineMovingChestDeep</waterMovingChestDeepTerrain>
    <foragedFood>RawBerries</foragedFood>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.1</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.12</plantDensity>
    <forageability>1.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>2</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/Wasteland</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>40</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>40</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>VolcanoSoil</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.5</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>WastelandAsphalt</terrain>
        <min>0.5</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>30</Clear>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>1.5</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>1</SnowHard>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">1</GrayPall>
      <ToxRain MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">4</ToxRain>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <RSW_FleeceSpider MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.7</RSW_FleeceSpider>  <!-- fleece spider - wretched-small, keep -->
      <RSW_BloodletterPetrel MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.7</RSW_BloodletterPetrel>  <!-- bloodletter petrel - wretched-small, keep -->
      <Borcatu MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.7</Borcatu>  <!-- Borcatu - wretched-small, keep -->
      <GR_Beetlefleet MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vgeneticse">0.7</GR_Beetlefleet>  <!-- beetlefleet - wretched-small, keep -->
      <GR_ParagonRat MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vgeneticse">0.7</GR_ParagonRat>  <!-- rodent paragon - wretched-small, keep -->
      <VFEI2_Swarmling MayRequire="oskarpotocki.vfe.insectoid2">0.6</VFEI2_Swarmling>  <!-- swarmlings - wretched-small, adjust-keep -->
      <AA_Eyeling MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.6</AA_Eyeling>  <!-- ikee - wretched-small, keep -->
      <VFEI2_BlackSwarmling MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.6</VFEI2_BlackSwarmling>  <!-- black swarmlings - wretched-small, adjust-keep -->
      <SW_Electrictick MayRequire="who.vfee.isopodageneline">0.5</SW_Electrictick>  <!-- Electrictick - extremophile-odd, adjust-keep -->
      <Toxalope MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.4</Toxalope>  <!-- toxalope - wretched-herd, import; vanilla Biotech animal, not mlie.advancedbiomes (DIRTY_CODE_REVIEW_STANDING_LOOP_1 wave: MayRequire pointed at an unrelated mod that happens to be active today but does not own this defName) -->
      <RSW_Maligoat MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Maligoat>  <!-- maligoat - wretched-herd, keep -->
      <RSW_Screecher MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Screecher>  <!-- screecher - wretched-pack, import -->
      <GR_Molebear MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vgeneticse">0.4</GR_Molebear>  <!-- molebear - wretched-medium, keep -->
      <GR_Spidercat MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vgeneticse">0.4</GR_Spidercat>  <!-- spidercat - wretched-medium, keep -->
      <!-- ROT_ROSTER_DEAD_DONOR_NAMES_1 (this pass): RSW_PustuleHornetQueen/
           RSW_ColonyPustuleHornetQueen/RSW_PustuleHornetSpawned removed — the
           owner's 2026-09-10 sitting ruled them "move" to the Rot
           (decisions_propagated.json), wasteland.json's roster no longer admits
           them, and they are now wired in RUT_TheRot.xml instead. Leaving them
           here too would have doubled a species the owner moved out. -->
      <AA_Terramorph MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_Terramorph>  <!-- terramorph - extremophile-odd, keep -->
      <VAEWaste_Megatardi>0.18</VAEWaste_Megatardi>  <!-- megatardi - extremophile-odd, import; STAT_NORM_WAVE2_RETIRE_1 absorbed this def natively into UtinniPatches itself (Defs/Absorbed_VAEWasteMegatardi/), so it needs no MayRequire on the retired donor mod at all. The old gate on vanillaexpanded.vaewaste (not in the live mod list) was silently dropping this animal from the roster every load (DIRTY_CODE_REVIEW_STANDING_LOOP_1 wave) -->
      <AA_AcanthamoebaGiganteaSmall MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_AcanthamoebaGiganteaSmall>  <!-- acanthamoeba gigantea, small - wretched-small, import -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <!-- wildPlants: transplanted from rosters/wasteland.json "flora" by
         BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1. This element was empty until now and the
         roster reached the game only through `BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml`'s replace
         operation, which is retired for biomes whose BiomeDef we author — so without
         this block the biome would have lost its flora outright.
         The roster is NINE rows, not the 25 the earlier note here claimed: eleven
         Polluted-Lands filler rows were cut 2026-09-18 (POLLUTED_LANDS_FLORA_PORT_1),
         and AB_ToxiGrass/PoisonPlantTallGrass went to the_blue_desert, PoisonShrub to
         the_propane_lakes, AB_GiantToxicFlower to poison_forest, PoisonPlantBush purged
         outright (all SHEET_ORPHAN_CONSUMPTION_1, owner ruling 2026-09-20).
         No MayRequire on any row. Eight are donor plants, and this folder's convention
         (and biome_flora.py's own documented reason) is that donor plants go unguarded
         because the def dump's packageId names the mod that last RETEXTURED a def, not
         the one that defines it. The ninth, RUT_ScorchedStars, is THIS mod's own def
         (Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RUT_PollutedFlora.xml) and so needs no guard either —
         same as its unguarded row in RUT_Scarlands.xml. -->
    <wildPlants>
      <RG_Plant_ToxiGrass>1.2</RG_Plant_ToxiGrass>  <!-- toxigrass -->
      <RG_Plant_TallToxiGrass>0.8</RG_Plant_TallToxiGrass>  <!-- tall toxigrass -->
      <Plant_GrayGrass>0.35</Plant_GrayGrass>  <!-- gray grass -->
      <RUT_ScorchedStars>0.3</RUT_ScorchedStars>  <!-- scorched stars -->
      <AB_WeepingToxberry>0.2</AB_WeepingToxberry>  <!-- weeping toxberry - tree -->
      <Plant_Toxipotato>0.2</Plant_Toxipotato>  <!-- toxipotato -->
      <AB_ToxiBulb>0.1</AB_ToxiBulb>  <!-- toxibulb -->
      <Plant_TreePolux>0.1</Plant_TreePolux>  <!-- polux tree - tree -->
      <VRE_PoluxBush>0.08</VRE_PoluxBush>  <!-- polux bush -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>15</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
